    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133">

                <pb facs="0139" n="133" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg133"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-11-24"><hi rendition="#italic">November 24,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s reply of the
                    21st of this month to your dispatch of the 11th instant, relative to the Bering
                    Sea seal question, I enclose for your information a copy of a letter from the
                    Acting Secretary of the Treasury, furnishing the information requested by you
                    regarding the number of seals taken on the Pribilof Islands.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>




